inflation in the united states just hit  9.1 percent it's a 40-year high and the  folks over on the all-in podcast we're  recently talking about has inflation  peaked or should we expect higher and  higher inflation in the coming months  chemoth palopatia had a great point  saying that a huge piece of the  inflation calculation comes from rent  and rent doesn't show up for a few  months he also pointed out that he  believes that inflation over nine  percent was a possibility and could even  see it going slightly higher but his big  takeaway was that we are in a sustained  inflationary environment here's what  chamoth had to say on the podcast you  know we talked about this that this was  going to be a big print right i think we  all expected this to be a big print i  actually also kind of put myself on a  limb there and i said you know i  wouldn't be surprised if at some point  we print a mid to high nines maybe even  a 10 handle at some point we're getting  there and the reason is because rents  are a little  you know uh they lag in how  they're reported inside of cpi so we  have a couple more months to go of of  rents and rents are moving or budging a  bit that's number one um we do see a  little bit of fall off in in energy  prices but i'm not so sure that it's  it's enough frankly to to move the  needle so i think that we could be in a  sustained period for a while after this  inflation print the expectation for july  went to 80 basis points from 75 which  means a small percentage of people  actually think it's going to be 100  and  september i think moved to 75. so the  question is is that enough i just don't  know i'm worried that we're in a  sustained inflationary environment i'm  worried about that i i hope that we're  not  now i tend to agree with chamoth but the  hard part about a lot of this  conversation is how do you define  sustained inflationary environment how  do you define whether inflation is  transitory or not there is no clear  definition what we know is that for the  last 12 months the united states economy  has experienced inflation over 5 percent  that alone i think proves that inflation  was not transitory and also that we are  in a sustained inflationary environment  the big question is how high can we go  we're at 9.1 percent now could we see  9.5 10 or higher no one knows the other  question is how long will this go on for  will this be a six month exercise 12  months 18 24 or longer the federal  reserve they understand the high  inflation has to come down and they're  doing everything in their power to get  it down they're raising interest rates  as aggressively as they can and they're  going ahead and trying to conduct  quantitative tightening by selling  assets off their balance sheet but at  the end of the day we are in a high  inflation environment no one knows how  high it can go and no one knows how long  it can last but a sustained inflationary  environment is not something that many  people were talking about or predicting  in january of 2020 fast forward two and  a half years later and here we are we  can look around the world for examples  of what happens in these situations if  you go to a place like argentina what  you see is things like price controls  and we've also seen here in the united  states many politicians talk about price  gouging or potential price controls now  i hope for the good of the people that  we don't actually get price controls  that we get inflation to come down and  that the federal reserve can navigate  this tough time without actually pushing  us into a recession it's a lot of ifs  and this is a highly complex situation  but i know that the people on the ground  the average american family they're  struggling right now seeing things like  9.1 percent official inflation is a bad  bad number and if it gets worse that  means there's only more pain to come the  solution hopefully won't be worse than  the problem but right now that problem  is eating away at the savings and wealth  of millions and millions of americans  and it is destroying the hard work and  economic value that those families have  put forward over the last few years  inflation hurts the average person and  we got to get it down 9.1 percent is a  crazy number but i'm with chamoth we're  in a sustained inflationary environment  how high it goes how long it lasts no  one knows  but we must act more aggressively to get  this down  because if not  we may just repeat the mistakes of other  countries that have had to endure  double-digit inflation for sustained  periods of time
 

